WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
A 12 volt battery, a 20 ohm
resistor and a large coil,

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.560
connected in one loop.

3
00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:11.050
In the end, the current
settles at 0.60 amps.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.580
But close the switch, and it
doesn't jump straight there.

5
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:19.860
After 25 milliseconds, it
has reached only 0.38 amps.

6
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.420
Why does the current take
time to reach its full value?

7
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.620
In this mission, you'll write
the loop rule for this circuit,

8
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.830
and solve it.

9
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.880
Then you'll take the battery away, and
follow the energy stored in the coil to

10
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.370
where it ends up.

11
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.270
Your mission: explain why the current
takes time to reach its full value.
